        "--prompt-en",
        "A complex dark-fantasy photograph of a consequential encounter, centered on the central fictional woman in a conquered river city's debt court after a lost war. Use the supplied reference as visible face and hair guidance for her: a short dark bob with a light separated fringe, soft rounded facial outline, dark eyes, and natural lips. She is an adult, formerly a minor noblewoman, now working as an occupation clerk. Her slightly frayed blue dress shows beneath a coarse gray work apron; the quiet beauty of her attentive face and composed bearing remains particular and human in this degrading office. She stands on the left behind a scarred desk inside a requisitioned chapel vestry. Opposite her, an older woman who once served her household waits in a rain-dark wool shawl with a linen ration sack against her hip. They meet each other's eyes with recognition held in check. The clerk's right hand presses an iron stamp vertically into warm amber wax on a release document. Her left forearm extends across the near edge of the desk, palm upward. A palm-sized split silver house-token rests across the two women's touching open left palms, the old emblem worn nearly smooth. The older woman's separate right forearm rests on the far side of the same desk, its iron debt cuff clearly exposed beside the open oath-ledger. A short ember-red filament runs from that cuff to the ledger across the dark tabletop. At the wax seal between them, the filament has just parted; both separated ends curl upward and fade, making the liberation visible at the instant of stamping. Keep the cuff, the ledger attachment, the intervening seal, and both newly separated ends readable together. Behind the clerk, a tired occupation auditor in a damp gray military coat watches the seal cool, one gloved hand resting beside a stack of confiscated house crests. His authority is ordinary and patient. Beyond the broken leaded window are floodwater, damaged roof timbers, and an abandoned siege hoist. A waist-up, medium-wide 3:2 view from the near corner of the desk places both women's faces, the stamp contact, and the shared token in one clear mid-depth plane. Their hands have room to act on separate parts of the tabletop. The auditor stays subordinate behind them. Cool overcast window light describes wet stone, worn cloth, skin texture, and tarnished silver; a small warm reflection from the wax touches the clerk's fingertips. Photograph the moment with restrained cinematic realism, natural human proportions, tactile weathered surfaces, and enough depth of field to read the connection between recognition, legal coercion, and the small act of release.",
